    {
      "id": "gv-823702-b00039",
      "text": "It is from the journey through melancholy that we reach Caminos citadinos y Pueblos Mágicos de México (City Roads and Magical Towns of Mexico). In this chapter, the poet shares some of the cities and towns that she has visited throughout her life and that are somehow significant, not for their touristic qualities, but for their historic and ancestral nature, as a part of Pasini's “Mexicanness,” and for the strategic connection with her soul.",
      "page": null,
      "paragraph": 39,
      "body_start": 3685,
      "body_end": 4130,
      "source_links": [],
      "source_kind": "p",
      "source_is_quotation": false
    },
